Ex. P16 - disability certificate records as under:
"i. Loss of vision in R-eye;
ii. Loss of hearing from left ear;
iii. Speech is unclear;
iv. Constants dribbling of saliva;
v. Deformities of face and facial expressions are abnormal;

vi. Weakness in L-upper and lower limb;
vii. Unable to walk;
viii. Forgetfulness, unable to correctly recollect the past events;
ix.

Presently she has post head injury;
ii. Hydrocephalus and thalamic calcification is due to old hematoma that is responsible for physical weakness, in-coordination of movements, partial loss of power in the limbs, unstable gait, etc causing physical impairment of basic movements like clothing, bathing, and toileting, combing hair or eating accounts for disability of 50%;
iii. Loss of hearing in both-ear is due to injury accounts for 20% cranial nerve impairment".
